  "privacy": "The records name real people as contacts. Every person's name, email address and phone number is replaced with a placeholder (Example Contact N, contact-N@example.com, 202-555-01NN). Each replacement keeps the value's type and format, and blank values stay blank, so neither check's outcome changes; expected below is measured on these files, and was the same on the original records. Company names, service descriptions, URLs and role mailboxes (such as security@<company>) are the providers' published business information and are kept.",
  "source_record_sha256_method": "SHA-256 of the original record as compact JSON: Python json.dumps(record, ensure_ascii=False, separators=(\",\", \":\")).",
  "expected_method": "DocumentValidationService.call(file bytes) with no format or document type named, so detection is checked too. Measured 2026-11-20 against the schemas vendored in lib/data/fedramp/schemas.",
